From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-cmake <v8-cmake@local>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Define __has_warning fallback for GCC

V8 15.x src/base/macros.h uses `defined(__has_warning) && __has_warning("...")`.
GCC does not provide __has_warning, and its preprocessor still parses the
right-hand operand even when the `defined(...)` guard short-circuits, failing
with "missing binary operator before token '('". Define the standard fallback
in v8config.h (included by macros.h) so such checks evaluate to 0 on GCC.
---
 v8/include/v8config.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/include/v8config.h b/v8/include/v8config.h
--- a/v8/include/v8config.h
+++ b/v8/include/v8config.h
@@ -24,6 +24,14 @@
 #include <memory>
 // clang-format off
 
+// GCC (unlike Clang) does not provide __has_warning. Define a fallback so
+// that checks such as `defined(__has_warning) && __has_warning("-Wfoo")`,
+// used in src/base/macros.h, compile on those toolchains instead of failing
+// preprocessing with "missing binary operator before token '('".
+#ifndef __has_warning
+#define __has_warning(x) 0
+#endif
+
 // Platform headers for feature detection below.
 #if defined(__ANDROID__)
 # include <sys/cdefs.h>
-- 
